# =============================================================================
# Trivy Ignore File – URA Chatbot
#
# Add CVE IDs or check IDs to suppress known false positives or accepted risks.
# Format: one ID per line, optional comment with # after.
# Docs: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids
#
# Review this file periodically – accepted risks may become patchable.
# =============================================================================

# ── Accepted Risks (document reason and review date) ─────────────────────────
# Example:
# CVE-2024-XXXXX  # Low-impact in our context; no patch until upstream release. Review: 2026-06-01

# ── Misconfiguration Suppressions ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Example:
# DS002  # Dockerfile: USER not set (we use non-root in runtime stage only)
